      "judge_rationale": "The summary accurately captures the book’s major claims and evidence: traditional (callous) toughness exemplified by Bobby Knight, Baumrind’s responsiveness/demandingness framework and authoritarian parenting harms, the Jordan McNair case and rhabdomyolysis risk, the contrast with humanistic coaches (Pete Carroll et al.), Self-Determination Theory (autonomy, competence, relatedness), psychological safety, reengagement, Viktor Frankl/meaning and PTG, and the harms of fear-driven motivation. It preserves most qualifiers (e.g., that punishment per se isn’t always bad; that real toughness is nuanced) and omits little low-value filler; presentation is clear and scannable. Deductions come from a few elements not supported (or not present) in the provided source/rubric: the explicit four-item “Four Pillars” list and the detailed personal case labeled as paradoxical vocal cord dysfunction (VCD) do not appear in the supplied source excerpt or rubric and seem to be added or overstated. Those invented or unsupported specifics reduce overall faithfulness and slightly affect qualifier preservation.",
